<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Murray and Roberts year earnings fall.</title>
<headline>Murray and Roberts year earnings fall.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     109	   vs   126</p>
<p>    Div (cts)   34 making 48.5	  vs   47.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   375	   vs   408</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-interest 703	   vs   733</p>
<p>    Tax			 128	   vs   151</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   182	   vs   120</p>
<p>Major contract provision</p>
<p>				  160	   vs    -</p>
<p>    Turnover	     10,746	   vs   9,283</p>
<p>Div payable October 18</p>
<p>on register September 20</p>
<p>Full name: Murray and Roberts Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The industrial holding company said it experienced lower than expected levels of activity and tighter margins in the period. M&amp;R has also set aside a 160 million rand provision following an ongoing dispute between Union Carriage &amp; Wagon and Siemens.</p>
<p>For the current year, the company said it expected a significant increase in earnings before interest and tax, but the level of attributable earnings and earnings per share would depend on the extent and timing of the continuing programme of dispasols of non-core activites.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast EPS in the year to June 30 or 113.0 cents, with the range 112.1-113.4.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
